  "system": {
    "identifier": "cloning-scout",
    "description": "<p>Bunshin</p>\n<p>Clone</p>\n<p>Armor Class Your Ninjutsu Save DC</p>\n<p>Hit Points 1</p>\n<p>Speed 30 ft.</p>\n<p>|  | Mod | Save |  | Mod | Save |  | Mod | Save |</p>\n<p>| STR | - | +0 | CON | - | +0 | WIS | - | +0 |</p>\n<p>| DEX | - | +0 | INT | - | +0 | CHA | - | +0 |</p>\n<p>Skills Uses Summoners Skills</p>\n<p>Senses Uses Summoner Senses</p>\n<p>Limited Casting. The Bunshin can cast 1 Jutsu from its casters known list after which, it is dispelled. This increases to 2 at 10th and 3 at 17th level. Bunshins can only make one attack with a jutsu per casting, regardless of the number of attacks a jutsu asks for and they can maintain concentration on jutsu they cast until the beginning of your next turn, after which they lose concentration.</p>\n<p>Placement. Bunshin you summon must be in a space within 60 feet of you.</p>\n<p>Basic Tools. The Bunshin has a basic version of one weapon its summoner has void of any weapon seals. It uses this weapon (If any) as part of its Bunshin strike. Its Bunshin Strike shares the range of this weapon. If no weapon, then it strike unarmed.</p>\n<p>Gang Up. When more than one Bunshin is attacking or targeting the same target, you do not make multiple attacks and the target does not make multiple saving throws, instead consolidate their attacks into a single attack roll or saving throw. Increase Bunshin Strike’s or Bunshins Cast damage by +4 for each Bunshin beyond the first.</p>\n<p>Hiding In Plain Sight. Bunshin are indiscernible from their summoner, so much so, that not even chakra sight can tell them apart. When one or more Bunshin are active, hostile creatures must perform the Search action at disadvantage vs the Summoners Stealth DC to determine that the Bunshins are clones.</p>\n<p>Attacks</p>\n<p>Bunshin Strike.  Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: + (Your Attack Bonus using the Bunshins cloned weapon) to hit, reach (weapons range)., one creature. Hit: 1d6 damage (weapons damage type).</p>\n<p>Bunshins Cast. The Bunshin casts a jutsu on its summoners known list of  C-Rank or lower that doesn’t have the Fuinjutsu or Combination keyword using the casters statistics to determine its attack bonus or save DC. If the jutsu deals damage, it deals an amount of damage equal to the rank the jutsu is cast at. (D-Rank: 2d6, C-Rank: 3d6, B-Rank: 4d6, A-Rank: 5d6,              S-Rank: 6d6).</p>\n<p>Those Scout-Nin that choose to become Cloning specialist employ superior numbers as their primary method of combat. They hone this skill through repeated use of their Clones in different situations allowing them to becomes masters of duplicative combat. Not every scout has the ability to use Clones the way a Cloning Scout can and it shows through their tactics and abilities available to them.</p>",
